  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/... \nThe subtropical ridge is still expected to weaken and shift back \neastwards by Friday according to ensembles. This is due to a \ntroughing pattern pushing into the NW CONUS and along the West \nCoast. As the trough pushes eastward, PWATs will begin to improve, \nreaching near 1.5\"-1.7\" by Saturday and lasting through at least the \nweekend. Mixing ratios will also significantly improve going from \nmid week's 6-8 g/kg to 10-12 g/kg by this weekend, generating better \nsupport for storm formation in the lower deserts. With that being \nsaid NBM/WPC continue to show PoPs over the weekend between 20-35% \nacross South-Central AZ, and now even up to 50% in the eastern high \nterrain. WIth these PoPs the NBM/WPC QPE totals over the weekend are \nforecasted between 0.10\"-0.25\" to locally higher in the higher \nterrain areas. Continued monitoring of this system will be needed \nbut models continue to show support for activity developing this \nweekend. In other good news, temperatures are forecast to drop \ncloser to late August normals by Sunday and into early next week as \nfalling midlevel heights and an increase in moisture/cloud cover \nover the eastern CWA support a cooling trend (more pronounced across \nSouth-Central AZ).",
